From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:17:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] core: keep the writable properties of Mutter's D-Bus services
 from sandboxed apps

GDBus asks g-authorize-method about method calls only, so a property
set through org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties went past
meta_dbus_guard_interface(). An app whose bus proxy lets it talk to a
name the shell owns could change the X11 scaling factor, or flip the
debugging switches, the one that turns off the accessibility services'
access control among them. The debugging switches, the devkit and the
profiler had no guard on their methods either.

meta_dbus_guard_property_writes() wraps the set_property of a skeleton
class, and refuses writes from every caller the instance's guard keeps
from its methods; an instance without a guard takes none. The debug
control and the display configuration, which had its own copy of this,
use it from their class, and meta_dbus_guarded_skeleton_new() makes a
guarded subclass on the spot for interfaces without a type of their
own, such as org.gnome.Mutter.X11. The devkit and the profiler get the
method guard with nothing open.

Upstream-Status: luft-only Luft's sandbox model; upstream leaves these services to the session bus
---
 src/backends/meta-display-config-skeleton.c |  49 +------
 src/core/meta-context.c                     |   2 +-
 src/core/meta-dbus-guard.c                  | 136 +++++++++++++++++++-
 src/core/meta-dbus-guard.h                  |   5 +
 src/core/meta-debug-control.c               |   5 +
 src/core/meta-mdk.c                         |   3 +
 src/core/meta-profiler.c                    |   6 +-
 src/core/meta-profiler.h                    |   4 +-
 src/x11/meta-x11-display.c                  |   5 +-
 9 files changed, 162 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

